  "summary": "Team Andromeda’s rail shooter pairs a dragon and rider with sweeping ruins, airborne machines and attacks arriving from every direction.",
  "body": [
    "Panzer Dragoon is Team Andromeda’s rail shooter, first released for Sega Saturn in Japan on 10 March 1995. A hunter becomes the rider of a blue dragon and pursues another dragon across the remains of an ancient civilisation. The flight follows a set route through three-dimensional environments, while the player moves the aiming reticle and shifts the dragon away from danger. Yukio Futatsugi directed the project, whose unfamiliar creatures, machinery and ruined landscapes gave one of Saturn’s early showcases a distinctive world of its own.",
    "Enemies can arrive ahead, beside or behind the dragon. The player turns the view to face them, using the radar to notice threats outside the current screen. A quick press fires the rider’s gun; holding the button while passing the reticle over targets prepares the dragon’s homing lasers. Releasing it sends the locked shots outward. The difference gives each weapon a practical role: a small exposed target may reward a quick shot, while a group approaching from different angles invites a sweep of the reticle.",
    "The predetermined flight lets each stage arrange a sequence of discoveries around the rider. Water, tunnels, ancient structures and huge airborne enemies come into view as the route advances, while the player continues aiming and dodging. Yoshitaka Azuma’s music accompanies that journey through a world whose history is also suggested by its surroundings. Jean Giraud, known as Moebius, illustrated the Japanese cover. The combination of a readable shooting system and a carefully presented setting established the series before Zwei expanded the flight and Saga changed its genre."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
